{"segs": ["PA_ja_84:0.2"], "en": "Ekakanipāta,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_84:0.3"], "en": "Apāyimhavagga", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_84:0.4"], "en": "4. The Atthasaddvāra Jātaka:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_84:1.1", "PA_ja_84:1.2"], "en": "“One should desire supreme health, gain, virtue approved by the elders, and learning.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_84:1.3"], "en": "“Conformity with the Dhamma and lack of dejection—", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_84:1.4"], "en": "these six are the foremost gateways to the goal.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_84:2.1"], "en": "Thus ends the fourth Jātaka, the Atthasaddvāra Jātaka.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"}
